rieve tags organized by series categories.\\n\\nThis endpoint returns a mapping of series categories to their associated tags, which can be used for filtering and search functionality.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/openapi.yaml get /search/tags_by_categories\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/search/get-tags-for-series-categories\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get Filters for Sports\",\"description\":\"Retrieve available filters organized by sport.\\n\\nThis endpoint returns filtering options available for each sport, including scopes and competitions. It also provides an ordered list of sports for display purposes.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/openapi.yaml get /search/filters_by_sport\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/search/get-filters-for-sports\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true}]},{\"group\":\"live-data\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"Get Live Data\",\"description\":\"Get live data for a specific milestone.\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/openapi.yaml get /live_data/milestone/{milestone_id}\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/live-data/get-live-data\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get Live Data (with type)\",\"description\":\"Get live data for a specific milestone. This is the legacy endpoint that requires a type path parameter. Prefer using `/live_data/milestone/{milestone_id}` instead.\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/openapi.yaml get /live_data/{type}/milestone/{milestone_id}\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/live-data/get-live-data-with-type\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get Multiple Live Data\",\"description\":\"Get live data for multiple milestones\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/openapi.yaml get /live_data/batch\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/live-data/get-multiple-live-data\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get Game Stats\",\"description\":\"Get play-by-play game statistics for a specific milestone. Supported sports: Pro Football, College Football, Pro Basketball, College Men's Basketball, College Women's Basketball, WNBA, Soccer, Pro Hockey, and Pro Baseball. Returns null for unsupported milestone types or milestones without a Sportradar ID.\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/openapi.yaml get /live_data/milestone/{milestone_id}/game_stats\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/live-data/get-game-stats\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get Event Live Data\",\"description\":\"Get live data for an event by its event ticker. Serves event-keyed live data such as crypto price charts, commodity price timeseries, and weather observations. The `type` field in the response names the schema of the `details` object.\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/openapi.yaml get /live_data/events/{event_ticker}\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/live-data/get-event-live-data\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get Weather Index\",\"description\":\"Get the Kalshi-computed city temperature index: the canonical minute-resolution series behind hourly temperature markets. City-keyed and independent of any event — the series exists whenever the city's index is configured. Values are Fahrenheit rounded to 0.01. Minutes where the index quorum failed carry no value and are never returned as points, so gaps in the series are real gaps. With `detailed=true` each point additionally carries every member station's reported reading and quality-control disposition — the pre-incorporation breakdown.\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/openapi.yaml get /live_data/weather/{city}\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/live-data/get-weather-index\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get Weather Index Calibrations\",\"description\":\"Get a city's published weather-index configuration timeline: the launch configuration plus every weekly offset calibration and methodology update, ascending by effective time. Each record carries the station weights, station offsets (Celsius), and the city reference used to compute index values from the record's effective time until the next record — everything needed to reproduce published index values for minutes computed under that configuration version. Offsets are re-estimated weekly after each complete UTC week; weights never change through calibration. The timeline is append-only and complete: it is never trimmed.\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/openapi.yaml get /live_data/weather/{city}/calibrations\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/live-data/get-weather-index-calibrations\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true}]},{\"group\":\"structured-targets\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"Get Structured Targets\",\"description\":\"Page size (min: 1, max: 2000)\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/openapi.yaml get /structured_targets\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/structured-targets/get-structured-targets\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get Structured Target\",\"description\":\" Endpoint for getting data about a specific structured target by its ID.\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/openapi.yaml get /structured_targets/{structured_target_id}\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/structured-targets/get-structured-target\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true}]},{\"group\":\"milestone\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"Get Milestone\",\"description\":\" Endpoint for getting data about a specific milestone by its ID.\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/openapi.yaml get /milestones/{milestone_id}\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/milestone/get-milestone\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get Milestones\",\"description\":\"Minimum start date to filter milestones. Format: RFC3339 timestamp\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/openapi.yaml get /milestones\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/milestone/get-milestones\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true}]},{\"group\":\"multivariate\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"Get Multivariate Event Collection\",\"description\":\" Endpoint for getting data about a multivariate event collection by its ticker.\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/openapi.yaml get /multivariate_event_collections/{collection_ticker}\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/multivariate/get-multivariate-event-collection\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Create Market In Multivariate Event Collection\",\"description\":\"Endpoint for creating an individual market in a multivariate event collection. This endpoint must be hit at least once before trading or looking up a market. Users are limited to 5000 creations per week.\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/openapi.yaml post /multivariate_event_collections/{collection_ticker}\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/multivariate/create-market-in-multivariate-event-collection\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get Multivariate Event Collections\",\"description\":\" Endpoint for getting data about multivariate event collections.\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/openapi.yaml get /multivariate_event_collections\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/multivariate/get-multivariate-event-collections\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true}]},{\"group\":\"incentive-programs\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"Get Incentives\",\"description\":\" List incentives with optional filters. Incentives are rewards programs for trading activity on specific markets.\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/openapi.yaml get /incentive_programs\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/incentive-programs/get-incentives\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true}]},{\"group\":\"fcm\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"Get FCM Orders\",\"description\":\"Endpoint for FCM members to get orders for their subtraders.\\nThis endpoint requires FCM member access level. At least one of `subtrader_id` or\\n`client_order_ids` is required; supplying both returns only the orders matching both filters.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/openapi.yaml get /fcm/orders\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/fcm/get-fcm-orders\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get FCM Positions\",\"description\":\"Endpoint for FCM members to get market positions filtered by subtrader ID.\\nThis endpoint requires FCM member access level and allows filtering positions by subtrader ID.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/openapi.yaml get /fcm/positions\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/fcm/get-fcm-positions\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true}]},{\"group\":\"historical\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"Get Historical Cutoff Timestamps\",\"description\":\"Returns the cutoff timestamps that define the boundary between **live** and **historical** data.\\n\\n## Cutoff fields\\n- `market_settled_ts` : Markets that **settled** before this timestamp, and their candlesticks, must be accessed via `GET /historical/markets` and `GET /historical/markets/{ticker}/candlesticks`.\\n- `trades_created_ts` : Trades that were **filled** before this timestamp must be accessed via `GET /historical/fills`.\\n- `orders_updated_ts` : Orders that were **canceled or fully executed** before this timestamp must be accessed via `GET /historical/orders`. Resting (active) orders are always available in `GET /portfolio/orders`.\\n- `market_positions_last_updated_ts` : Settled positions **archived from the live data set** before this timestamp must be accessed via `GET /historical/positions`. Unsettled positions are always available in `GET /portfolio/positions`.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/openapi.yaml get /historical/cutoff\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/historical/get-historical-cutoff-timestamps\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get Historical Market Candlesticks\",\"description\":\" Endpoint for fetching historical candlestick data for markets that have been archived from the live data set. Time period length of each candlestick in minutes. Valid values: 1 (1 minute), 60 (1 hour), 1440 (1 day).\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/openapi.yaml get /historical/markets/{ticker}/candlesticks\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/historical/get-historical-market-candlesticks\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get Historical Fills\",\"description\":\" Endpoint for getting all historical fills for the member. A fill is when a trade you have is matched.\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/openapi.yaml get /historical/fills\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/historical/get-historical-fills\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get Historical Orders\",\"description\":\" Endpoint for getting orders that have been archived to the historical database.\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/openapi.yaml get /historical/orders\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/historical/get-historical-orders\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get Historical Positions\",\"description\":\" Endpoint for getting settled market positions that have been archived to the historical database. Positions whose markets were archived before `market_positions_last_updated_ts` on `GET /historical/cutoff` are available via this endpoint. Positions are archived per whole event: a settled event's positions move here together and are never split between this endpoint and `GET /portfolio/positions`. Unsettled positions are always available via `GET /portfolio/positions`.\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/openapi.yaml get /historical/positions\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/historical/get-historical-positions\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get Historical Trades\",\"description\":\" Endpoint for getting all historical trades for all markets. Trades that were filled before the historical cutoff are available via this endpoint. Block trades are included by default and identified by the `is_block_trade` field; use the `is_block_trade` query parameter to filter by block / non-block. See [Historical Data](https://docs.kalshi.com/getting_started/historical_data) for details.\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/openapi.yaml get /historical/trades\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/historical/get-historical-trades\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get Historical Markets\",\"description\":\"Endpoint for getting markets that have been archived to the historical database. Filters are mutually exclusive.\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/openapi.yaml get /historical/markets\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/historical/get-historical-markets\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"Get Historical Market\",\"description\":\" Endpoint for getting data about a specific market by its ticker from the historical database.\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"openapi\":\"/openapi.yaml get /historical/markets/{ticker}\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/historical/get-historical-market\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true}]}]},{\"group\":\"CF Benchmarks REST\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"CF Benchmarks REST Passthrough\",\"description\":\"Query CF Benchmarks REST data using your existing Kalshi API credentials\",\"href\":\"/cfbenchmarks/rest-passthrough\"}]},{\"group\":\"WebSockets\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"WebSocket API\",\"description\":\"Trade API WebSocket endpoint and schema reference\",\"href\":\"/websockets\"},{\"title\":\"WebSocket Connection\",\"asyncapi\":\"asyncapi.yaml root\",\"description\":\"Main WebSocket connection endpoint. All communication happens through this single connection.\\nAuthentication is required to establish the connection; include API key headers during the WebSocket handshake.\\nSome channels carry only public market data, but the connection itself still requires authentication.\\nUse the subscribe command to subscribe to specific data channels. For more information, see the [Getting Started](https://docs.kalshi.com/getting_started/quick_start_websockets) guide.\\n\",\"href\":\"/websockets/websocket-connection\"},{\"title\":\"Connection Keep-Alive\",\"asyncapi\":\"asyncapi.yaml control_frames\",\"description\":\"WebSocket control frames for connection management.\\n\\nKalshi sends Ping frames (`0x9`) every 10 seconds with body `heartbeat` to maintain the connection.\\nClients should respond with Pong frames (`0xA`). Clients may also send Ping frames to which Kalshi will respond with Pong.\\n\",\"href\":\"/websockets/connection-keep-alive\"},{\"title\":\"Orderbook Updates\",\"asyncapi\":\"asyncapi.yaml orderbook_delta\",\"description\":\"Real-time orderbook price level changes. Provides incremental updates to maintain a live orderbook.\\n\\n**Requirements:**\\n- Authentication required\\n- Market specification required:\\n  - Use `market_ticker` (string) for a single market\\n  - Use `market_tickers` (array of strings) for multiple markets\\n  - `market_id`/`market_ids` are not supported for this channel\\n- Sends `orderbook_snapshot` first, then incremental `orderbook_delta` updates\\n- Supports `update_subscription` with `add_markets` / `delete_markets` / `get_snapshot` actions\\n- `get_snapshot` returns an `orderbook_snapshot` for the requested `market_tickers` without modifying the subscription\\n\\n**Use case:** Building and maintaining a real-time orderbook\\n\",\"href\":\"/websockets/orderbook-updates\"},{\"title\":\"Market Ticker\",\"asyncapi\":\"asyncapi.yaml ticker\",\"description\":\"Market price, volume, and open interest updates.\\n\\n**Requirements:**\\n- No additional channel-level authentication beyond the authenticated WebSocket connection\\n- Market specification optional (omit to receive all markets)\\n- Supports `market_ticker`/`market_tickers` and `market_id`/`market_ids`\\n- Updates sent whenever any ticker field changes\\n\\n**Use case:** Displaying current market prices and statistics\\n\",\"href\":\"/websockets/market-ticker\"},{\"title\":\"CF Benchmarks Value Feed\",\"asyncapi\":\"asyncapi.yaml cfbenchmarks_value\",\"description\":\"$4b\",\"href\":\"/websockets/cfbenchmarks-value\"},{\"title\":\"CF Benchmarks 5Hz Value Feed\",\"asyncapi\":\"asyncapi.yaml cfbenchmarks_value_5hz\",\"description\":\"$4c\",\"href\":\"/websockets/cfbenchmarks-value-5hz\"},{\"title\":\"Pyth Value Feed\",\"description\":\"Real-time Pyth price updates for configured underlying tickers\",\"asyncapi\":\"asyncapi.yaml pyth_value\",\"href\":\"/websockets/pyth-value\"},{\"title\":\"Public Trades\",\"asyncapi\":\"asyncapi.yaml trade\",\"description\":\"Public trade notifications when trades occur.\\n\\n**Requirements:**\\n- No additional channel-level authentication beyond the authenticated WebSocket connection\\n- Market specification optional (omit to receive all trades)\\n- Updates sent immediately after trade execution\\n\\n**Use case:** Trade feed, volume analysis\\n\",\"href\":\"/websockets/public-trades\"},{\"title\":\"User Fills\",\"asyncapi\":\"asyncapi.yaml fill\",\"description\":\"Your order fill notifications. Requires authentication.\\n\\n**Requirements:**\\n- Authentication required\\n- Market specification optional via `market_ticker`/`market_tickers` (omit to receive all your fills)\\n- Supports `update_subscription` with `add_markets` / `delete_markets`\\n- Updates sent immediately when your orders are filled\\n\\n**Use case:** Tracking your trading activity\\n\",\"href\":\"/websockets/user-fills\"},{\"title\":\"Market Positions\",\"asyncapi\":\"asyncapi.yaml market_positions\",\"description\":\"Real-time updates of your positions in markets. Requires authentication.\\n\\n**Requirements:**\\n- Authentication required\\n- Market specification optional (omit to receive all positions)\\n- Filters are by `market_ticker`/`market_tickers` only; `market_id`/`market_ids` are not supported\\n- Updates sent when your position changes due to trades, settlements, etc.\\n\\n**Monetary Values:**\\nAll monetary values are returned as fixed-point dollar strings (`_dollars` suffix).\\n\\n**Use case:** Portfolio tracking, position monitoring, P\u0026L calculations\\n\",\"href\":\"/websockets/market-positions\"},{\"title\":\"Market \u0026 Event Lifecycle\",\"asyncapi\":\"asyncapi.yaml market_lifecycle_v2\",\"description\":\"Market state changes and event creation notifications.\\n\\n**Requirements:**\\n- No additional channel-level authentication beyond the authenticated WebSocket connection\\n- Receives all market and event lifecycle notifications (`market_ticker` filters are not supported)\\n- Event creation notifications\\n\\n**Use case:** Tracking market lifecycle including creation, de(activation), close date changes, determination, settlement, price level structure changes, and metadata updates\\n\",\"href\":\"/websockets/market-and-event-lifecycle\"},{\"title\":\"Multivariate Market \u0026 Event Lifecycle\",\"asyncapi\":\"asyncapi.yaml multivariate_market_lifecycle\",\"description\":\"Multivariate event (MVE) market state changes and event creation notifications.\\n\\n**Requirements:**\\n- No additional channel-level authentication beyond the authenticated WebSocket connection\\n- Receives all multivariate market lifecycle notifications (`market_ticker` filters are not supported)\\n- Only emits lifecycle updates for multivariate events\\n- Event creation notifications\\n\\n**Use case:** Tracking multivariate market lifecycle including creation, de(activation), close date changes, determination, settlement\\n\",\"href\":\"/websockets/multivariate-market-and-event-lifecycle\"},{\"title\":\"Communications\",\"asyncapi\":\"asyncapi.yaml communications\",\"description\":\"Real-time Request for Quote (RFQ) and quote notifications. Requires authentication.\\n\\n**Requirements:**\\n- Authentication required\\n- Market specification ignored\\n- Optional sharding for fanout control:\\n  - `shard_factor` (1-100) and `shard_key` (`0 \u003c= key \u003c shard_factor`)\\n- RFQ events (RFQCreated, RFQDeleted) always sent\\n- Quote events (QuoteCreated, QuoteAccepted, QuoteExecuted) are only sent if you created the quote OR you created the RFQ\\n\\n**Use case:** Tracking RFQs you create and quotes on your RFQs, or quotes you create on others' RFQs. Use QuoteExecuted to correlate fill messages with quotes via client_order_id.\\n\",\"href\":\"/websockets/communications\"},{\"title\":\"Order Group Updates\",\"asyncapi\":\"asyncapi.yaml order_group_updates\",\"description\":\"Real-time order group lifecycle and limit updates. Requires authentication.\\n\\n**Requirements:**\\n- Authentication required\\n- Market specification ignored\\n- Updates sent when order groups are created, triggered, reset, deleted, or have limits updated\\n\\n**Use case:** Tracking order group lifecycle and limits\\n\",\"href\":\"/websockets/order-group-updates\"},{\"title\":\"User Orders\",\"asyncapi\":\"asyncapi.yaml user_orders\",\"description\":\"Real-time order created and updated notifications. Requires authentication.\\n\\n**Requirements:**\\n- Authentication required\\n- Market specification optional via `market_tickers` (omit to receive all orders)\\n- Supports `update_subscription` with `add_markets` / `delete_markets` actions\\n- Updates sent when your orders are created, filled, canceled, or otherwise updated\\n\\n**Use case:** Tracking your resting orders, fills, and cancellations in real time\\n\",\"href\":\"/websockets/user-orders\"}]},{\"group\":\"FIX\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"Common Components\",\"description\":\"Standard header, trailer, and shared components across all FIX messages\",\"icon\":\"puzzle-piece\",\"href\":\"/fix/common-components\"},{\"title\":\"Connectivity\",\"description\":\"Endpoints, transport configuration, and rate limits for the Kalshi FIX API\",\"icon\":\"network-wired\",\"href\":\"/fix/connectivity\"},{\"title\":\"Authentication \u0026 Sessions\",\"description\":\"API key creation, logon, session lifecycle, and message retransmission\",\"icon\":\"key\",\"href\":\"/fix/authentication\"},{\"title\":\"Order Entry\",\"description\":\"Submit, modify, and cancel orders through FIX messages\",\"